# /etc/apex/guest-accounts — accounts that may be wiped at session end.
#
# One account name per line. `#` starts a comment; blank lines are ignored.
#
# THIS FILE SHIPS EMPTY, AND THAT IS THE POINT. /usr/libexec/apex-guest-wipe
# refuses every account that is not named here — it does not guess from a name
# prefix, a uid range or a home directory, because every one of those rules
# matches somebody's real account on some machine. An APEX with no guest
# configured cannot be talked into wiping anything, whatever it is handed.
#
# Adding a line here does NOT create the account, does not enable a guest
# session, and does not wipe anything on its own. It says: if the wipe runs for
# this account, it is allowed to. See
# /usr/share/apex/shared-machine/README.md for the rest of the recipe.
#
# Never put the machine owner's account in this file.
